- NFS Server -
NFS Export
The export on the NFS server, for example /srv/ps2, or / for the whole server. RiptOPL speaks NFS version 4.0 on port 2049.
NFS Writes
Off: RiptOPL only reads the export, whatever the server allows, keeps game settings next to its own and uses no VMC there. On: renaming, deleting, saving and VMCs on the export, where the server allows it.
%d: Cannot connect to NFS server. It must offer NFS version 4.0 on port 2049.
%d: The NFS server refused this PS2.
%d: Cannot open the NFS export. Check NFS Export and the server address.
This Neutrino has no NFS support -- launching with the OPL core.
Neutrino cannot write a VMC on the NFS export -- launching with the OPL core.
These NFS settings are beyond Neutrino's limits -- launching with the OPL core.
NFS Writes is Off, so no VMC can be used on the export. The game saves to the real memory card.
POPSTARTER cannot launch over NFS. Use Ember, or SMB, for this game.
NFS Writes is Off, so Ember cannot keep memory card saves in this game's folder.
